cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this work, please use the metadata below."
title: "FlyBrain: teaching a 27-cell mushroom-body model to read, and proving what it cannot read"
abstract: >-
  A spiking classifier whose only plastic synapses are the 13,824 KC->MBON
  weights of a simplified mushroom-body model, trained on a hand-drawn 5x7
  bitmap alphabet with three-factor reward-modulated STDP. The circuit reaches
  100.0% holdout accuracy on 27 symbols (26 letters plus a blank) and is then
  shown ten digits it has no output cell for. It answers all 300 digit
  presentations with a letter, gets 0 correct, and its weight matrices and
  checkpoint are byte-identical before and after - the negative control is
  hashed rather than asserted. No connectome is used; the package docstring
  says so explicitly.
authors:
  - name: "Ascendstarcel"
type: software
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-31"
keywords:
  - spiking neural network
  - mushroom body
  - reward-modulated STDP
  - three-factor learning
  - optical character recognition
  - negative control
  - reproducibility

repository-code: "https://github.com/Ascendstarcel/FruitFlyBrain_AlphabetTrainings"
